  "notes": "Digitized from the Kodak E-7020 datasheet of December 2017. Kodak: \"for making direct digital prints from digital files, as well as optical prints from color negatives\", \"enhanced color reproduction\"; named first by Gold 200's (E-7022, 2023) and UltraMax 400's (E-7023, 2016) sheets. Process RA-4 at 100 F (38 C), 45 s; the sheet gives no sensitometric exposure time. The characteristic curves are drawn in short pieces, chained end to end. Status A curves; the enlarger is the same stand-in as ENDURA Premier's. No granularity and no MTF on the sheet. G ends highest, then R, then B, as the labels at the curves' ends stand.",
